  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Each shared hand tool has a numbered hook and a matching sign-out line; borrowing ends within the member’s booked session.\", \"decision\": \"How should shared hand tools be checked out?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers write their names on the sign-out line before removing shared hand tools from the numbered hooks. Other members can locate borrowed tools directly and know who is responsible for returning them.\nMembers put a named borrowing card on the numbered hook when taking a shared hand tool. The empty hook itself identifies the borrower, so someone seeking that tool can find the current user.\nThe steward records each requested hand tool on the sign-out line and hands it to the borrowing member. A single handover links the tool’s location and borrower without asking members to update records themselves."
    }
  ],
